th new flag parsing and field handling logic. Looking at the next phase, I need to implement key-based sorting functionality by extending the existing sort command to handle field definitions, extract specific fields from records, and compare them according to the key specifications outlined in the SRD requirements R2.2 through R3.1. .3 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd053-sort requirement R2.4 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd053-sort requirement R3.1 as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing comparison logic to support key-based field extraction\n      - id: D2\n        text: Target LC_ALL=C locale behavior only per project architecture decision DD6\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/sort compiles with go build -o bin/sort ./cmd/sort/\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/sort/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Requirements R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, and R3.1 from srd053-sort.yaml are implemented as specified\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Previously implemented functionality (R1.1-R1.7, R2.1) is preserved\n\nNow I'm moving to the next task which focuses on numeric sort modes and check/merge functionality, building on the existing sort implementation to handle requirements R3.2 through R4.1. Now I'm checking the acceptance criteria for the implementation—verifying that the sort command compiles cleanly, passes linting checks, and that the new numeric comparison requirements are properly implemented while preserving all previously working functionality. I'm verifying the file paths are correct—the SRD is at `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-sort.yaml` and the use case at `docs/specs/use-cases/rel07.0-uc001-sort.yaml`. I should note in the response that tasks for R4.2-R4.4 and the tr/tail requirement are deferred to future batches, then finalize the output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":n